{"topic": "graduation rates", "review": {"readability_score": 4, "source_accuracy_score": 3, "qualification_retention_score": 3, "unsupported_claims": ["\"on-time graduation within 150% of normal time\": 150% is beyond normal time, so \"on-time\" mislabels the measure.", "\"Rates are ready-made, and underlying counts include transfer-out and gender and race detail\" is stated for the whole 150% area. Transfer-out and gender/race detail are supported for some tables (GR2015-GR2024 and the DRVGR tables), but the 2-year 100%-completion counts are not available by race/ethnicity or gender.", "\"Compare cohorts by Pell Grant and subsidized loan receipt\" blurs the Subsidized Stafford and Direct Subsidized Loan series into one label. The sources do not establish that they are equivalent, and the \"subsidized loan\" wording implies they are.", "\"Cohort counts for students whose gender was unknown or another gender\" is grouped under \"Financial aid and gender detail\", which suggests a link to financial aid. The gender table covers only two outcome years (2022, 2023) and has no completion information.", "\"Eight-year bachelor's rates\" is given as an example of 200% of normal time. This is supported for 4-year institutions only, and the sentence does not say so.", "The Outcome Measures point says \"entering undergraduates\" generally, but the table covers only the 2008 cohort. Its four cohorts are full-time first-time, part-time first-time, full-time non-first-time and part-time non-first-time, while the \"share ... earned an award\" and enrollment variables cited are full-time, first-time only.", "\"Outcome dates across these sources: August 31, 2015 through 2024\" implies uniform coverage. The Pell/loan series, the gender series and Outcome Measures cover much narrower ranges."], "missing_qualifications": ["Institution coverage per area is dropped: 4-year vs 2-year vs less-than-2-year vs less-than-4-year.", "The Pell/Stafford series covers outcome dates 2016-2022 and the Direct Subsidized series 2023-2024; the candidate gives no separate year filters.", "The gender-unknown series covers only the 2022 and 2023 outcome dates.", "The 200% series spans mixed cohort years (4-year 2006, 2008-2016), with no cohort versus outcome-date distinction.", "The Outcome Measures cohort is 2008 only, with a single 2016 outcome status date (six-year status is as of 2014)."], "comments": ["The prose is clear and concise, and the required qualification sentences are present. They are appended as a block rather than attached to the relevant points.", "Citations are present, but several claims they back are broader than the quotes. For example, R135851P2 supports 4-year bachelor's counts, not the \"eight-year rates\" claim by itself.", "Moving the exhaustive detail to Definitions & sources is acceptable, but period and institution scope for the narrower series should have been stated briefly."]}}
